course: dictionary
lesson: 6483
title: Navigation: finding your way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Navigation is the skill or process of finding your way or planning a route, especially at sea or in the air. «The Māori arrived in Aotearoa, New Zealand, from Polynesia about 700 years ago and are famous for ... their navigation.» Arriving from far away means crossing the ocean, so navigation here means their skill at finding a way across the water.
explain: The words around a word are its context. «By the 11th century compasses were used for navigation at sea.» A compass shows direction, and «at sea» tells you where. So navigation means finding the way on the water. Check by swapping in your meaning: "compasses were used for finding your way at sea" still makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. On a ship, navigation can mean steering it. On a website, the navigation is the menu of links. A sat nav in a car is a navigation system that shows the way. Context tells you which meaning you need.
fact: Navigation means the skill or process of finding your way or planning a route.
fact: «Navigation» can mean steering a ship or plane.
fact: On a website, the navigation bar is its menu and links, which help you move around.
fact: A sat nav is a navigation system that shows you the way, often in a car or on a phone.
fact: «The Māori» are famous for their navigation, as well as carving, tattooing and the haka.
exercise: «By the 11th century compasses were used for navigation at sea.» What is navigation in this sentence? | Painting pictures of waves | *Finding your way across the sea | A kind of fish | Cooking food on a boat
exercise: A sat nav in a car is a... | A type of car engine | A kind of song | *A system that shows you the way | A paper map of the moon
exercise: On a website, the navigation bar is... | *Its menu and links that help you move around | Ocean waves | A bicycle | A football pitch
test: The Māori are famous for their navigation. What is that skill? | Making tattoos | *Finding their way across the ocean | Carving wood by hand | Singing the haka
test: Navigation has more than one meaning. Which one is about steering a ship? | *Steering a ship or plane | Menu links on a website | Taking photos | A list of music tracks
exam: Ella says, «My sat nav told me to turn left at the next corner.» What does sat nav mean here? | *A system that shows her the way | Ella's favourite radio station | A type of sandwich | A kind of pet
